  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 2.48,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings rise exponentially (doubling time about 1 h) and then stop suddenly at about 0.63–0.67 from 7 h on. A plateau that sharp suggests the reader is saturating rather than the culture reaching stationary phase. Diluted retained aliquots confirm this. At 18 h, a 10× dilution read 0.2513 and 0.2504, which corrects to about 2.51. A 20× dilution read 0.1157 and 0.1297, which corrects to about 2.45. The two dilutions agree, so the diluted reads are in the reader's proportional range. A single 10× read at 12 h gave 0.2488, about 2.49, so the culture was already about 2.5 during the plateau. A single 10× read at 6 h gave 0.044, about 0.44, against 0.379 undiluted. This one read suggests the reader may start to under-report even around 0.4, but it could also be noise. The undiluted plateau of about 0.65 is therefore an artefact of the reader, and the real biomass over the final hours is about 2.5 OD600-equivalents, roughly 3.8× higher than the undiluted readings show. The 12 h and 6 h results each come from a single read."
  },
